      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bound readModelRunImageFiles with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`readModelRunImageFiles` in `src/cli/capability-cli/model.ts:88` reads user-supplied `--file` CLI argument image files into memory with no size limit. A user passing a multi-GB file to `openclaw model run` would OOM the process before the MIME type check.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nUnbounded `fs.readFile` on user-controlled paths is a valid OOM vector. Model run images are user-supplied CLI inputs — multi-GB files are not legitimate inputs for model vision features.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded `readModelRunImageFileSafely` helper with a `statSync` size pre-check:\n1. Stats the resolved path\n2. Rejects non-regular files\n3. Rejects files exceeding 100 MiB cap\n4. Only reads files that pass the checks\n\n## Evidence\n\n100 MiB is well above any legitimate model run image input (typical images are 0.1-10 MiB, even high-res screenshots are under 50 MiB). The cap prevents OOM on accidentally selected large files or malicious input.",
